     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. The patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO two or three times daily**, which are common regimens.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is really what you intend, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
